 "headline": "File prefetch is not the lever: a learned BM25 + potion-code-16M-v2 fusion finds the files that matter (edited-file recall@5 0.70-0.74, @10 0.86-0.89, transfers leave-one-repo-out), but a one-shot path hint at the prompt saves only +4.0% of $ [3.2, 4.8] / +1.6 calls per task at p_follow=1 (+1.9% [1.5, 2.3] at 0.5) on held-out Haiku, the oracle ceiling with per-target re-hints is 11.9% of $, content preloading loses 34-37%, targeted line ranges net +1.8%, and unmeasured misfire reads can flip the sign.",
